  "id": "USN-8625-1",
  "summary": "openssl vulnerability",
  "details": "It was discovered that OpenSSL incorrectly allocated memory buffers in the\nSSL/TLS state machine when receiving handshake data. A remote attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause OpenSSL to consume excessive memory,\nleading to a denial of service. This issue is known as the \"HollowByte\"\ndenial of service.",
